@startuml class_ports
title MicroserviceBase - Port Interfaces (post-migration, 2026-05-07)

skinparam class {
    BackgroundColor<<abstract>> #CCCCFF
    BackgroundColor<<service>> #CCE5FF
    BackgroundColor<<legacy>> #DDDDDD
}

note as N1
  **Architecture status**
  - **HubManagerPort** is the canonical orchestration interface.
    NomadHubAdapter (current) and LocalHubManager (legacy)
    both implement it.
  - **TransportPort / ServiceRegistryPort** retain their
    broker vocabulary (consume / exchange / routing_key).
    They are still used by legacy services; new services
    talk gRPC + Consul directly via runtime / grpc_bridge
    code paths and do not depend on these ports.
  - **UIBridgePort** is current — FastAPIBridge implements
    it and serves both the Manager GUI and any browser /
    Electron client.
end note

package "ports" {

    abstract class HubManagerPort <<abstract>> {
        {abstract} +start_hub(mode, **kwargs): dict
        {abstract} +stop_hub(): dict
        {abstract} +get_status(): dict
        {abstract} +start_processes(names): dict
        {abstract} +stop_processes(names, force): dict
        {abstract} +get_config(): dict
        {abstract} +add_config(name, config): dict
        {abstract} +update_config(name, config): dict
        {abstract} +remove_config(name): dict
        {abstract} +get_service_log(name, tail): dict
        {abstract} +import_service(name, source_path, zip_data, wait_time): dict
        {abstract} +remove_service(name): dict
        {abstract} +reset(): dict
    }

    abstract class UIBridgePort <<abstract>> {
        {abstract} +start(request_handler, services_info_provider)
        {abstract} +stop()
        {abstract} +broadcast_update(services_info)
    }

    abstract class TransportPort <<legacy>> {
        {abstract} +connect()
        {abstract} +disconnect()
        {abstract} +stop_consuming()
        {abstract} +consume(service_name, routing_key, exchange, handler)
        {abstract} +rpc_call(request_data, exchange_name, routing_key): dict
        {abstract} +publish(exchange, routing_key, body, properties)
    }

    abstract class ServiceRegistryPort <<legacy>> {
        {abstract} +register(service_info)
        {abstract} +unregister(service_info)
        {abstract} +subscribe_to_events(handler)
        {abstract} +notify_update(services_info)
        {abstract} +get_update_channel_name(): str
    }

    note right of HubManagerPort
      Backend-agnostic orchestration interface (ADR-022).
      Same surface used by the FastAPI bridge whether the
      backend is a single-host Nomad client (dev) or a
      multi-node Nomad cluster (production, ADR-024).
    end note

    note right of UIBridgePort
      ``request_handler`` routes ServiceRequest → ServiceResponse.
      ``services_info_provider`` returns the current discovery
      view — for new services this is sourced from Consul,
      for legacy services from the in-process ServiceRegistry.
      ``broadcast_update()`` pushes to all connected UI clients.
    end note

    note bottom of TransportPort
      Broker-era port (RabbitMQ AMQP).  Vocabulary
      (exchange / routing_key / consume) doesn't fit
      gRPC.  New services bypass this port and use
      grpc_bridge / runtime_cpp directly.
    end note

    note bottom of ServiceRegistryPort
      Broker-era port — superseded by Consul (ADR-023).
      Still implemented by AMQPRegistryAdapter so legacy
      services keep working during the migration window.
    end note
}

package "domain  <<legacy>>" {

    class ServiceBase <<legacy>> {
        -_transport: TransportPort
        -_registry: ServiceRegistryPort
        +serve()
        +register_service()
        +request_service()
    }
}

' Dependency direction: domain depends on ports (inward)
ServiceBase --> TransportPort : depends on
ServiceBase --> ServiceRegistryPort : depends on

@enduml
